&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;ZoomInfo is where careers accelerate. We move fast, think boldly, and empower you to do the best work of your life. You’ll be surrounded by teammates who care deeply, challenge each other, and celebrate wins. With tools that amplify your impact and a culture that backs your ambition, you won’t just contribute. You’ll make things happen–fast.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div&gt;As a&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Software Engineer III on the Developer Productivity team&lt;/strong&gt;, you&#39;ll help build systems on our Python-based agentic platform that turn inputs such as Jira tickets, Slack conversations, help-desk requests, and CRM signals into clearly scoped, human-supervised engineering work—then help implement, review, and improve that work.&lt;br&gt;You&#39;ll contribute to systems that clarify problem statements, generate implementation plans, run a conversational Slack intake experience, and assist engineers with repository discovery, plan execution, testing, and pull request creation. You&#39;ll also help build the platform behaviors—permissions, auditability, evaluation, observability, rollback, and cost controls—that make all of this dependable at scale.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The Developer Productivity team owns the tooling, automation, and standards that make engineers across ZoomInfo more productive, and is becoming the company&#39;s center of gravity for AI-assisted development. You&#39;ll be working within an ecosystem of internal developer platforms, PR and workflow automation tools, and AI devex tooling that spans code review, dependency management, and agent orchestration.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Our engineering culture values diversity, intellectual curiosity, problem-solving, and openness. We encourage collaboration, big thinking, and calculated risk-taking in a blame-free environment. You&#39;ll have the opportunity to work on meaningful projects while receiving the support and mentorship needed to grow your career..&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help design and build systems that convert bug reports and feature requests into clarified problem statements, implementation plans, and approval gates before any execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to a conversational Slack intake experience that notifies the right people, asks targeted follow-up questions, converts confirmed requirements into Jira, and hands work to the delivery workflow&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help normalize additional sources of demand—such as help desk, Salesforce, or operational alerts—while preserving provenance, urgency, ownership, and customer context&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build tooling that assists engineers with implementation: repository discovery, plan execution, automated testing, pull request creation, and concise evidence of what changed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to automated pull request review for correctness, regressions, test coverage, maintainability, and policy concerns, while keeping merge approval with people&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help build the platform behaviors that make agentic workflows dependable: permissions, auditability, evaluation, observability, rollback, and cost controls&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverage AI-powered development tools (such as Claude, Cursor, GitHub Copilot) to accelerate development, improve code quality, and solve complex technical challenges&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with cross-functional teams to define, design, and ship new features&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write clean, maintainable, and well-tested code following best practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in code reviews and share knowledge with teammates&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Troubleshoot and resolve issues across distributed, agentic systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Computer Science, a related field, or equivalent practical experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3-5 years of backend software development experience, with strong proficiency in Typescript, NodeJs, and ReactJS&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing and troubleshooting distributed systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with RESTful API design and microservices architecture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with relational and NoSQL databases (e.g. MongoDB)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity integrating third-party APIs (e.g., Jira, Slack, Salesforce)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with cloud platforms (AWS, GCP, or Azure)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Master&#39;s degree in Computer Science or Engineering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience building or working with LLM-based or agentic systems (agent orchestration, tool-calling, evaluation frameworks)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with AI-assisted development tools (Claude, Cursor, GitHub Copilot, or similar platforms)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with internal developer productivity platforms—data pipelines/lakes, PR automation and AI code review tooling, dependency management automation, or similar&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Node.js or Java for backend development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of containerization and orchestration (Docker, Kubernetes)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with CI/CD pipelines and observability/monitoring practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LI-SK1&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LI-Hybrid&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Actual compensation offered will be based on factors such as the candidate’s work location, qualifications, skills, experience and/or training. Your recruiter can share more information about the specific salary range for your desired work location during the hiring process. We want our employees and their families to thrive.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In addition to comprehensive benefits we offer holistic mind, body and lifestyle programs designed for overall well-being. Learn more about ZoomInfo benefits &lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; href=&quot;https://www.zoominfo.com/careers#benefits&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://www.zoominfo.com/careers#benefits&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Below is the US base salary for this position. Additional compensation such as Bonus, Commission, Equity and other benefits may also apply.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$112,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$176,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About us:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;ZoomInfo (NASDAQ: GTM) is the Go-To-Market Intelligence Platform that empowers businesses to grow faster with AI-ready insights, trusted data, and advanced automation. Its solutions provide more than 35,000 companies worldwide with a complete view of their customers, making every seller their best seller.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;ZoomInfo is committed to protecting your privacy when you apply for jobs with us. Please review our Job Applicant &lt;a href=&quot;https://drive.google.com/file/d/1yiG-k0YX_sW10PiJk_xliDc3W-veJCrK/view?usp=drive_link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt; for more details on how we handle your personal information.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;ZoomInfo may use a software-based assessment as part of the recruitment process. More information about this tool, including the results of the most recent bias audit, is available &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.zoominfo.com/legal/nyc-local-law-144-notice&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;ZoomInfo is proud to be an equal opportunity employer, hiring based on qualifications, merit, and business needs, and does not discriminate based on protected status. We welcome all applicants and are committed to providing equal employment opportunities regardless of sex, race, age, color, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity, marital status, disability status, religion, protected military or veteran status, medical condition, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. We also consider qualified candidates with criminal histories in accordance with legal requirements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For Massachusetts Applicants: It is unlawful in Massachusetts to require or administer a lie detector test as a condition of employment or continued employment. An employer who violates this law shall be subject to criminal penalties and civil liability. ZoomInfo does not administer lie detector tests to applicants in any location.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;div&gt;Attentive® is the AI marketing platform for 1:1 personalization redefining the way brands and people connect. We’re the only marketing platform that combines powerful technology with human expertise to build authentic customer relationships. By unifying SMS, RCS, email, and push notifications, our AI-powered personalization engine delivers bespoke experiences that drive performance, revenue, and loyalty through real-time behavioral insights.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Recognized as the&amp;nbsp;#1&amp;nbsp;provider in SMS Marketing by G2, Attentive partners with more than 8,000 customers across 70+ industries. Leading global brands like Crate and Barrel, Urban Outfitters, and Carter’s work with us to enable billions of interactions that power tens of billions in revenue for our customers.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;With a distributed global workforce and employee hubs in New York City, San Francisco, London, and Sydney, Attentive’s team has been consistently recognized for its performance and culture. We’re proud to be included in&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.deloitte.com/content/dam/assets-zone3/us/en/docs/services/deloitte-private/2025/us-2024-technology-fast-500-rankings.pdf&quot;&gt;Deloitte’s Fast 500&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;(four years running!),&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.attentive.com/blog/attentive-ranked-8-on-linkedins-2020-top-startups-list-in-the-united-states&quot;&gt;LinkedIn’s Top Startups&lt;/a&gt;,&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.forbes.com/lists/cloud100/&quot;&gt;Forbes’ Cloud 100&lt;/a&gt; (five years running!),&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.inc.com/best-workplaces/2025&quot;&gt;Inc.’s Best Workplaces&lt;/a&gt;, and the&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.hrc.org/resources/corporate-equality-index&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Human Rights Campaign Foundation&#39;s Corporate Equality Index&lt;/a&gt;!&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The &lt;strong&gt;Staff Software Engineer on the platform team&lt;/strong&gt; will help set the technical direction for the compute and networking platform that underpins Attentive’s microservices architecture. The role involves building reusable cloud components, clear interfaces, and self-service tools that make infrastructure easier to use and safer to operate.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This hands-on technical leadership role drives measurable improvements in platform reliability, cost efficiency and developer productivity. Responsibilities span identifying shared needs across teams, setting architectural direction, and leading complex initiatives from problem definition through production operation, balancing delivery speed with security and long-term maintainability&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The platform runs on AWS and uses Kubernetes, Istio, Argo CD, Terraform, and Cloudflare at the edge.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Accomplish&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape the technical direction and architecture of Attentive’s platform as part of the compute and networking team, partnering with engineering leaders to prioritize investments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with engineering teams to understand their workflows and pain points, and build platform software, APIs, and self-service tools that reduce friction and help them deliver reliable services faster.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead complex initiatives across teams, turning ambiguous requirements into designs, delivery plans, and measurable outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evolve Kubernetes and networking infrastructure across multiple AWS accounts and networks to support growth, resilience, and efficient resource use.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and improve Infrastructure-as-Code orchestration and reusable cloud components, providing consistent interfaces and guardrails for consuming AWS services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Diagnose complex production issues and drive lasting improvements to system design, observability, and operational practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve platform reliability, scalability, and cost efficiency while reducing operational overhead for the platform team and its users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Raise the engineering bar through hands-on development, design and code reviews, mentorship, and technical guidance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and establish effective AI-assisted engineering practices across the team, improving productivity while maintaining code quality, security, and operational reliability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Expertise&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Significant experience designing, building, and operating large-scale infrastructure or distributed systems, with demonstrated technical leadership across teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong software engineering background, including building maintainable software, tooling, or APIs that solve infrastructure problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to independently identify opportunities, bring clarity to ambiguous problems, and lead complex technical initiatives through delivery and production ownership, adapting to evolving needs and shaping technical direction in a fast-changing environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated customer empathy, with the ability to translate developer feedback and observed pain points into platform improvements and assess success through adoption, ease of use, and customer outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to evaluate architectural tradeoffs, communicate decisions clearly, and build alignment across teams with different needs and priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep experience with AWS or a comparable cloud platform, Infrastructure as Code, and building reusable infrastructure abstractions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Substantial experience operating Kubernetes in production, including an understanding of its architecture, networking, and failure modes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of networking fundamentals across L3–L7 and experience diagnosing complex connectivity, routing, DNS, load-balancing, and service-to-service communication issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in release engineering, including designing and improving CI/CD pipelines, automating software and infrastructure delivery, and enabling safe deployments through testing, staged rollouts, and reliable rollback and recovery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using observability to understand system behavior, troubleshoot production issues, and guide reliability improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using AI-assisted development tools to accelerate implementation, testing, debugging, and documentation, with sound judgment in validating generated code and protecting sensitive information.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commitment to mentorship, constructive feedback, and continuous learning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll get competitive&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.attentive.com/benefits&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;perks and benefits&lt;/a&gt;, from health &amp;amp; wellness to equity, to help you bring your best self to work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;For US based applicants:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The US base salary range for this full-time position is $200,000 - $230,000 annually&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;+ equity + benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Our salary ranges are determined by role, level and location&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 255, 255);&quot;&gt;#LI-MN1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;By applying for this position, your data will be processed as per &lt;a href=&quot;https://drive.google.com/file/d/1RViE_YUnu0ipiJQ9xDpC-iSJ9sYJBbX8/view?usp=sharing&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Attentive&#39;s Privacy Policy&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Attentive Company Values&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Default to Action&lt;/strong&gt; - Move swiftly and with purpose&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Be One Unstoppable Team&lt;/strong&gt; - Rally as each other’s champions&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Champion the Customer &lt;/strong&gt;- Our success is defined by our customers&#39; success&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Act Like an Owner&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;- Take responsibility for Attentive’s success&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Learn more about &lt;a class=&quot;postings-link&quot; href=&quot;https://www.attentive.com/awake&quot;&gt;AWAKE&lt;/a&gt;, Attentive’s collective of employee resource groups.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;If you do not meet all the requirements listed here, we still encourage you to apply! No job description is perfect, and we may also have another opportunity that closely matches your skills and experience.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;At Attentive, we know that our Company&#39;s strength lies in the diversity of our employees. Attentive is an Equal Opportunity Employer and we welcome applicants from all backgrounds. Our policy is to provide equal employment opportunities for all employees, applicants and covered individuals regardless of protected characteristics. We prioritize and maintain a fair, inclusive and equitable workplace free from discrimination, harassment, and retaliation. Attentive is also committed to providing reasonable accommodations for candidates with disabilities. If you need any assistance or reasonable accommodations, please let your recruiter know.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Senior Full Stack Engineer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About LaunchDarkly Engineering&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;LaunchDarkly helps engineering organizations &lt;a href=&quot;https://launchdarkly.com/pa/b/hpselectorb/?utm_source=google&amp;amp;utm_medium=cpc&amp;amp;utm_campaign=AMS_Search_Brand_pltf&amp;amp;utm_adgroup=Brand_Feature-Flag&amp;amp;utm_content=hpselectorb&amp;amp;utm_term=launchdarkly%20feature%20flag&amp;amp;matchtype=p&amp;amp;creative=825840905025&amp;amp;device=c&amp;amp;_bt=825840905025&amp;amp;_bn=g&amp;amp;gad_source=1&amp;amp;gad_campaignid=24291558199&amp;amp;gbraid=0AAAAADk9kA8O0dYcZS-ouv7zdVBdKH2rx&amp;amp;gclid=CjwKCAjww-3VBhAcEiwAwUUIuxsMpjalsFeTe7g_tWSHfLPKBQH1zXJEi8z6_GmZz36GhK3l9Q5gchoCE6YQAvD_BwE&quot;&gt;ship software and AI with speed&lt;/a&gt;, safety, and control. Our platform gives teams the confidence to release gradually, target experiences to the right audiences, learn through experimentation, understand what is happening in production, and respond quickly when risk appears.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our engineers build the systems, services, SDKs, developer tools, cloud infrastructure, and product experiences that make this possible. The work spans high-scale distributed systems, reliable data and event pipelines, intuitive enterprise workflows, and AI-powered capabilities that help teams manage the next generation of software delivery.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;LaunchDarkly’s SDKs are used in systems that perform trillions of feature flag evaluations each day, giving our engineering work a direct connection to the reliability and customer experience of software around the world. As the company grows, we are expanding beyond traditional feature management into experimentation, observability, and AgentControl—helping customers control more of the software and AI lifecycle. That creates an unusually broad set of technical challenges, visible customer impact, and room for engineers to shape what comes next.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe in the power of teams. We work with humility, openness, curiosity, and care; we value clear communication, thoughtful technical judgment, inclusive collaboration, and a strong sense of ownership. We encourage people to apply even when they do not meet every qualification listed below. We are interested in the experience, perspective, and potential you would bring to the role.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The specific technical emphasis will vary by opportunity. Some teams may prioritize backend depth, data-intensive applications, enterprise workflows, observability, experimentation, or AI-powered product experiences. Senior scope at LaunchDarkly is defined by sustained impact, technical judgment, and influence beyond an individual feature—not by years of experience alone.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Full Stack Engineer at LaunchDarkly, you will lead the design and delivery of customer-facing product experiences and the backend systems that support them. You will work across the application boundary from intuitive, accessible interfaces to reliable services, APIs, and data flows—and help shape how customers understand, configure, and control software delivery.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is an opportunity to own complex, high-impact work where engineering judgment is visible. You will partner closely with Product, Design, Data, Staff Engineers, Engineering Managers, and adjacent teams to make complex capabilities feel clear and useful, while ensuring that the underlying systems are scalable, secure, observable, and dependable. Your technical decisions will influence both the product experience and the systems that enable it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the design and delivery of large or ambiguous end-to-end initiatives across frontend and backend systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop product experiences using technologies such as &lt;strong&gt;TypeScript and React&lt;/strong&gt;, along with services and APIs using technologies such as &lt;strong&gt;Go, Python,&lt;/strong&gt; or comparable tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate customer problems and product goals into thoughtful technical designs, clear tradeoffs, and incremental delivery plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own work from discovery and design through implementation, launch, measurement, operational support, and iteration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product, Design, Data, and engineering leaders to balance usability, accessibility, performance, reliability, security, cost, and time to value.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish patterns and practices that improve consistency, maintainability, developer experience, and quality across the product.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve observability and operational health across the frontend and backend systems you touch, and participate in incident response when needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Influence architecture and technical direction through design documents, code reviews, technical discussions, and clear written and verbal communication.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor engineers and help teammates grow their technical judgment, product instincts, and ability to deliver end-to-end work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent customer needs and production realities in cross-functional decisions, and connect technical work to measurable outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of experience building and operating production web applications, with a track record of delivering meaningful customer or business impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to lead complex projects across frontend and backend layers, including ambiguous requirements or cross-team dependencies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong experience with a modern frontend framework such as &lt;strong&gt;React &lt;/strong&gt;and a typed language such as &lt;strong&gt;TypeScript,&lt;/strong&gt; or equivalent experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong backend experience designing or operating APIs, services, data stores, or asynchronous systems in a production environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with a backend language such as&lt;strong&gt; Go,&lt;/strong&gt; Python, Rust, or an equivalent language. &lt;strong&gt;(Most of our teams use Go)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sound judgment across architecture, user experience, accessibility, performance, reliability, security, and maintainability tradeoffs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong product instincts and the ability to connect technical decisions to customer outcomes and business goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to create alignment with engineers and cross-functional partners through clear communication and inclusive decision-making.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience mentoring engineers, improving team practices, and raising the quality of technical execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong sense of ownership for the full lifecycle of the systems and experiences you help build.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort learning unfamiliar systems and navigating changing priorities with curiosity and a collaborative mindset.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pay:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Target pay ranges based on Geographic Zones* for Level 4:&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;ul1&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Zone 1: &lt;em&gt;San Francisco/Bay Area or NYC Metropolitan Area, Boston, Seattle&lt;/em&gt; - $191,800 - $263,670 **&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Zone 2:&lt;em&gt; Irvine, LA, Monterey, Santa Barbara, Santa Rosa, Austin, Portland, Philadelphia, Chicago - &lt;/em&gt;$172,600 - $237,270 **&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Zone 3: &lt;em&gt;All other US locations - &lt;/em&gt;$163,000 - $224,070**&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;LaunchDarkly operates from a place of high trust and transparency; we are happy to state the pay range for our open roles to best align with your needs. Exact compensation may vary based on skills, experience, and location.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;*Within the United States, our geographic pay zones are defined by counties surrounding major metropolitan areas.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;**Restricted Stock Units (RSUs), health, vision, and dental insurance, and mental health benefits in addition to salary.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About LaunchDarkly:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Modern software delivery was supposed to be the foundation for a thriving digital business but reality has proven otherwise. Slow, inefficient development cycles, costly outages, and fragmented customer experiences are preventing developers from building their best software. The LaunchDarkly platform helps developers innovate on new features faster while protecting them with a safety valve to instantly rewind when things go wrong. Developers can target product experiences to any customer segment and maximize the business impact of every feature. And by gradually rolling out new application components, they escape nightmare &quot;big-bang&quot; technology migrations.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The LaunchDarkly platform was built to guide engineers to the next frontier of DevOps by:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improving the velocity and stability of software releases, without the fear of end customer outages&lt;/li&gt;
